# The version of the cross-implementation vector corpus that vectors/ holds.
#
# The corpus is owned by timeflareio/chain (testdata/vectors/). Normally this
# file holds a chain release tag (e.g. v0.1.0) and `make vectors-verify`
# checks the vendored copy against that release's SHA-256 manifest.
#
# Right now it holds a monorepo commit instead, because this repo was lifted
# before the chain repo existed to publish anything (multi-repo migration plan,
# phase 1). `make vectors-verify` is inert while the pin has this shape and
# says so rather than passing silently. It becomes a real check when the chain
# repo cuts its first release and this file moves to that tag — phase 2b.
#
# The flip is a formality, not a risk: all other work is frozen for the
# duration of the migration, so the corpus this copy came from and the corpus
# chain will publish are the same bytes.
